The top-level decision remains **NARROW**. `fresh_readonly_worker_v1` is an **ephemeral one-shot independence profile**, not a persistent Agent Session.

## Current Temporary Chat launch/delivery contract

```text
prepared/open generic delegation
 -> neutral ChatGPT preflight URL with one preflight nonce
 -> exact runtime-attested MV3 service worker receives private run/correlation handoff
 -> one live owner record binds owner_tab_id + private run + exact correlation + task URL
 -> authenticated loopback request/response binding to the exact local controller
 -> controller commit attempted
 -> success OR ambiguous commit acknowledgement
 -> same live owner reconciles exact durable commit via authenticated private-token /status
 -> only that original neutral preflight tab may location.replace(task URL)
 -> task URL carries opaque launch handle only
 -> same live MV3 lifetime resolves handle -> private run capability
 -> exact live composer == intended worker prompt
 -> fresh/non-personalized/no-plugin child qualification
 -> one IndexedDB browser delivery claim
 -> one project-local delivery claim
 -> exactly one Send authority
 -> exact live composer is rechecked immediately before click
 -> delivered | unknown
 -> same-delivery reconciliation
 -> exact WORKER_RESULT_V1 capture when trustworthy result is present
```

The private durable `run_id` is absent from task/browser-history URL state, worker prompt and IndexedDB delivery claim. The legacy fragment field name `cap_run_id` carries only the opaque live launch handle.

PowerShell opens **only the neutral preflight**. It is not a second task-navigation owner. `launch.json` is evidence/status projection. The same live preflight tab navigates with `location.replace()` only after exact commit/reconciliation proof.

Complete browser/MV3 lifetime loss remains fail closed and cannot reconstruct launch/Send/monitor authority.

## Exact source execution contract

Physical qualification does not trust mutable post-gate worktree bytes as the effectful runtime source:

```text
clean exact-HEAD provenance gate
 -> git archive <EXPECTED_HEAD> runtime/
 -> record + lock archive SHA-256
 -> derive expected extension hashes from archive entries
 -> materialize extension snapshot from that archive
 -> hold selected archive/extension/input files read-share-only
 -> build one explicitly Windows-quoted Python argument line
 -> start Python with -I -B -S
 -> import controller/runtime only from the exact archive via zipimport/runpy
 -> prove the pinned 127.0.0.1:3078 exact authenticated controller is live and owns the pinned listener
 -> browser runtime attestation must match the same archived extension bytes
 -> extension/controller traffic must satisfy the authenticated loopback protocol
```

## Physical-A finding history and current fixes

The first target-Windows A attempt on reviewed HEAD `31b6f045f0f2b31388d40bbb573cf8df4490af58` correctly failed before Send. Live ChatGPT exposed both an empty generic `textarea` and the actual prompt editor. The old selector-list lookup could bind the empty textarea first, so the exact-composer gate saw an empty prompt and never requested Send authority.

HEAD `2895dd0f...` repaired that physical failure by preferring the prompt editor over the generic textarea, but the next fresh semantic review found one surviving P1: selector-class priority could still bind a hidden/stale exact-prompt editor while a different visible current editor would actually be submitted.

Current HEAD `0c1afc0371d0e074d500afd6bfe5b02fae894957` addresses that P1 narrowly:

- editor lookup is scoped to the same Send-button composer;
- all candidate `#prompt-textarea`, contenteditable and textarea descendants are enumerated;
- disconnected/hidden/`aria-hidden`/disabled candidates are rejected;
- Send authority proceeds only when exactly one live visible editable candidate remains;
- multiple visible candidate editors fail closed before authority;
- the same helper is reused for immediate-pre-click exact prompt revalidation and post-delivery cleanup;
- regression coverage includes both the real hidden generic-textarea failure and stale/hidden or multiply-visible competing editors;
- extension execution generation was recomputed to bind the changed runtime bytes.

Focused local tests on clean exact HEAD passed before push:

- `test_chatgpt_temporary_prompt_source_provenance.py` — 8/8;
- `test_chatgpt_temporary_extension_contract.py` — 17/17;
- `test_chatgpt_temporary_execution_generation.py` — 3/3;
- `test_chatgpt_temporary_post_delivery_guard.py` — 6/6;
- `test_chatgpt_temporary_post_delivery_uninterrupted.py` — 1/1.

The fresh semantic review on `2895dd0f...` is now historical because HEAD moved to fix its confirmed P1.

